# Q8: append results/recipe/caveats to /output/report.json
import json
p='/output/report.json'; r=json.load(open(p))
A=lambda n,v:{"name":n,"value":v}
common=[A("data","pbcor cubes Xb55 (2-1), Xb47 (4-3), Xb4f/Xb4d/Xb4b (3-2); moment-0 |v-2780|<350 km/s; exact beam-difference smoothing kernels (scripts/matched.py); positions N (0,+2.55\"), S (-0.15,-2.55\"), Bridge (+0.3,+0.15\") from the Q1 deblend"),A("flux scale","10% per OUS; cancels in N/S contrasts (same maps), not in absolute ratios"),A("errors","statistical only (null-window rms of the smoothed map); no deblend: values are position samples of blended maps")]
def R(q,v,u,unit,conf,ev,tgt,extra=()):
    r['results'].append({"quantity":q,"value":v,"uncertainty":u,"unit":unit,"confidence":conf,"evidence":ev,"target":tgt,"assumptions":common+list(extra)})
R("Q8a: N/S ratio of T43/T32 (Tb, matched beam, no deblend) HCN, by which array supplies the 3-2",
  "Xb4f 3-2 (+Xb47 4-3), beam 6.2x3.7\": N 0.425, S 0.319, Bridge 0.364 -> N/S 1.33, N/Bridge 1.17, S/Bridge 0.88 (circ 6.5\": 1.19; 9.5x6.4\": 1.26). Xb4d 3-2 (+Xb47): N 0.486, S 0.443 -> N/S 1.10 (6.5\": 1.02). Xb4b 3-2: N 0.537, S 0.531 -> 1.01 (6.5\": 1.03). At the Xb47 beam 4.4x3.0\": Xb4d 1.10, Xb4b 0.97. The team-b p0015 value 1.26+-0.09 is reproduced only with Xb4f as the 3-2 source; with the higher-resolution arrays the contrast is 0.97-1.10 (consistent with 1).",
  "statistical +-0.02-0.04 on each ratio; the spread among 3-2 arrays (0.97-1.33) is the systematic and is 5-10x the statistical error","ratio","low","out/q8/T43_T32_contrast.csv; scripts/q8_matched.py, q8_contrast.py","N, S, Bridge")
R("Q8b: N/S ratio of T43/T32 HCO+ (matched beam, no deblend)",
  "Xb4f 3-2: N 0.547, S 0.483 -> N/S 1.13 (circ 6.5\": 1.09; 9.5x6.4\": 1.11). Xb4d 3-2: 1.00-1.01 at every beam. Xb4b 3-2: 0.89-0.98 (S higher). So HCO+ shows no N/S contrast except with Xb4f as 3-2 source, and then only 1.1.",
  "+-0.01-0.02 statistical; spread 0.89-1.13","ratio","low","out/q8/T43_T32_contrast.csv","N, S")
R("Q8c: array-to-array recovery of the 3-2 line flux at matched beam (extended-gas loss, N vs S)",
  "At the Xb4f beam, 3-2 flux of Xb4d/Xb4f: HCN N 0.88, S 0.72, Bridge 0.81; HCO+ N 0.87, S 0.78, Bridge 0.82. Xb4b/Xb4f: HCN N 0.79, S 0.60, Bridge 0.65; HCO+ N 0.80, S 0.65. S loses 18-24% (HCN) / 11% (HCO+) more extended flux than N in the Xb4d data relative to Xb4f. Continuum (same frequency, no line contamination): Xb4d/Xb4f N 0.85, S 0.78, Bridge 0.80 (N/S double ratio 1.10). Recovery therefore differs between N and S by 10-20% and moves T43/T32 N/S by the same amount whenever the 3-2 and 4-3 images do not share uv coverage.",
  "+-0.01 statistical; the Xb47 4-3 recovery relative to Xb4f is NOT measurable in the archive: contrast correction between 1.0 and the Xb4d-like 1.22 (HCN) / 1.12 (HCO+) is unconstrained","ratio","medium","out/q8/recovery_32_arrays.csv, out/q8/continuum_matched.csv; scripts/q8_contrast.py, q8_cont_recovery.py","N, S, Bridge")
R("Q8d: Is the HCN T43/T32 N/S excess a Tkin effect or a recovery/size effect? (answer)",
  "Not established as Tkin. If the Xb47 4-3 loses extended flux like Xb4d (S more than N), the 1.33 shrinks to 1.09; if it is as complete as Xb4f the contrast stays 1.2-1.33 (HCN) and 1.1 (HCO+). Pure size/filling difference with equal intrinsic excitation (compact+extended Gaussians with the measured N/S sizes) gives HCN contrast 1.02-1.13 (median; 84th percentile up to 1.4 for the extreme r_c=1, r_ext=0.25); P(contrast >= 1.33) = 0.0-0.23 (0.04-0.11 for r_ext~0.36); HCO+ 0.98-1.0 (obs 1.13: P 0-0.23). If the 4-3 is more compact than 3-2 (size x0.7) the size-only contrast is <1 (0.8-0.9), so size alone cannot make N look more excited. Taken at face value (Xb4f), a contrast of 1.33 corresponds at equal density to T_N/T_S ~ 1.5-1.9 (e.g. 37 vs 22 K at n=1e6, N(HCN)=10^15.5; 66 vs 36 K at 3e5), or at equal T to a 0.2-0.4 dex higher n (HCO+) -- Tkin and n are degenerate in the ratio. Overall: tentative N>S excitation, size effect disfavoured as the sole cause, recovery systematic not excluded.",
  "contrast statistical +-0.04; size-only P values from importance-sampled growth-curve posteriors (4000 draws); inversion at logN 15-16","","low","out/q8/size_only_forward.csv, out/q8/tkin_vs_density_inversion.csv; scripts/q8_forward.py","N, S",
  [A("size model","compact+extended Gaussians fitted to the 3-2 peak-Tb growth curve (Xb4b/Xb4d/1.7\"/Xb4f; the same data as Q12c: double use), r_compact 0.6-1.0 (1.0 = RJ thick limit), r_ext 0.25-0.45 (Bridge-like 0.36/0.48)"),A("excitation","RADEX LVG grids out/q4c/grid4_*.npz, Tbg 2.73 K, shared beam filling for both lines")])
R("Q8e: per-line source size, filling and compact share of the 3-2 peak Tb, N/S (3-2 growth curve)",
  "Compact FWHM: N HCN 0.43\" [0.27,0.55], HCO+ 0.43\" [0.24,0.57]; S HCN 0.34\" [0.28,0.42], HCO+ 0.37\" [0.30,0.45]. Extended FWHM: N 4.5-4.7\" [2.3,13], S 12-13\" [7,20]. Beam filling of the compact component (peak): N HCN 0.76 (0.25\"), 0.21 (Xb4d), 0.016 (Xb47 4.2x2.7\"), 0.009 (Xb4f), 0.003 (Xb55); S HCN 0.67, 0.15, 0.010, 0.006, 0.002. Compact share of the 3-2 peak Tb: N HCN 0.77 (Xb4d), 0.28 (Xb47), 0.21 (Xb4f); HCO+ 0.64, 0.17, 0.13; S HCN 0.79, 0.23, 0.16; HCO+ 0.77, 0.21, 0.14. Extended-filling u (Q12c): N 1.6 [1.1,3.0], S 1.1 [1.04,1.3]. Only the 3-2 sizes are measured; 2-1 and 4-3 sizes are not measurable (the 4-3 ladder has a single beam). Bridge has no compact peak fit (its 3-2 Tb is nearly beam-independent between 4\" and 9\" at the matched beams: extended-dominated); its filling is not fitted.",
  "16-84% in brackets; HCN and HCO+ sizes agree within the errors","arcsec / fraction","medium","out/q8/filling_by_beam.csv, out/q12c/geometry.csv; scripts/q8_forward.py","N, S")
R("Q8f: continuum check of N-vs-S recovery/spectral-index (Xb47/Xb4f at matched beam)",
  "Continuum Xb47(346.5 GHz)/Xb4f(257.7 GHz) at 6.2x3.7\": N 2.29, S 1.91, Bridge 2.18 (N/S 1.20). If recovery were equal the implied spectral indices are N 2.8, S 2.2, Bridge 2.6; the continuum N/S double ratio 1.20 is the same size as the HCN T43/T32 excess (1.33 / 1.2), i.e. the 'excess' also appears in the line-free continuum where it is a spectral-index/recovery/free-free effect, not gas excitation. Degenerate: cannot separate alpha from recovery.",
  "statistical <1%; interpretation ambiguous","ratio","low","out/q8/continuum_matched.csv; scripts/q8_cont_recovery.py","N, S, Bridge",[A("assumption","same-frequency Xb4d/Xb4f ratio measures pure array recovery; Xb47/Xb4f differs by (346.5/257.7)^alpha x recovery")])
r['recipe'].append({"order":len(r['recipe'])+1,"stage":"modelling","description":"Q8: matched-beam T43/T32 without deblend (4.4x3.0\", Xb4f 6.2x3.7\", circ 6.5\", Xb55 9.5x6.4\" beams, exact kernels) with 3-2 from Xb4b, Xb4d and Xb4f; array recovery ratios of 3-2 and of the continuum; size-only forward model (compact+extended Gaussian posteriors, r_c 0.6-1, r_e 0.25-0.48, 4-3 size x1 or x0.7); RADEX inversion of the ratio at logN 15-16.","scripts":["scripts/q8_matched.py","scripts/q8_contrast.py","scripts/q8_cont_recovery.py","scripts/q8_forward.py","scripts/build_report_q8.py"]})
r['interpretation']+=("\n\nQ8: The only surviving N-vs-S temperature signal (T43/T32 N/S 1.26-1.33 HCN, 1.1-1.13 HCO+, team-b p0015) depends on which array supplies the 3-2: with the Xb4f 3-2 it is 1.33 (HCN) at the exact Xb4f beam, with Xb4d/Xb4b 3-2 it is 0.97-1.10. The arrays recover different amounts of extended 3-2 flux at S than at N (S loses 11-24% more), so a differential recovery between Xb47 and Xb4f of this size would remove the contrast; the continuum shows the same N/S 1.2 factor between Xb47 and Xb4f. A pure size/filling difference at equal excitation produces at most ~1.1 (P(>=1.33) <= 0.1 for plausible excitation), so the contrast is not a size effect either: it is either a modest real excitation difference (T_N/T_S ~1.5-1.9 at equal n if taken at face value; degenerate with n) or a recovery/spectral-index systematic. Conclusion: tentative, not demonstrated; the research question's N-vs-S temperature difference has no supported answer at this resolution. A matched ~1\" 1-0 (or 2-1 at Xb4d resolution) map from the same array would give a third ladder step observed with common uv coverage and break the n-T degeneracy; it is not in the archive.")
r['caveats'].append("Q8: the T43/T32 contrasts are position samples of blended maps (no deblend); the Xb47 4-3 recovery relative to Xb4f/Xb4d is not measurable here (only 3-2 and continuum can be compared across arrays); size-only forward model double-uses the 3-2 growth curve and assumes identical sizes for 3-2 and 4-3 (x1) or 4-3 30% smaller; RADEX inversion uses one-zone grids with shared filling; absolute ratios carry a 10% scale per OUS (14% on a ratio). The N-vs-S Tkin conclusion is therefore low confidence.")
json.dump(r,open(p,'w'),indent=1)
